Every window is generated from its own body and its own script. The html
platform caches what does not vary by window (the analysis, the __n* id map,
the esbuild bundle) across the whole compilation, so a page taking another
page's cached work is exactly the failure this guards against: each page must
carry its own text and its own updater, and none of the others'.

alpha is declared first, so it is generated first and fills the caches the
other three read.

delta declares no state and no handler, so its page is the one that shows what
a window inherited that is not its own: the analysis a window mutates during
codegen (which helper functions its script needs, which CSS its components
registered) is per-window, and only the package-derived half is shared. A leak
here would give delta another window's runtime.

Which window is generated first must decide nothing but that. The same four
declared in the opposite order are generate_multi_window_content_reversed.txtar.

deny out/none/html/index.html `beta body` -- alpha is generated first and fills the caches; there is nothing yet for it to take another window's static text from
deny out/none/html/index.html `beta shows` -- nor another window's reactive text, which is the per-window half of the analysis
deny out/none/html/index.html `gamma body` -- same for gamma's static text
deny out/none/html/index.html `gamma shows` -- same for gamma's reactive text
deny out/none/html/beta.html `alpha body` -- beta reads the caches alpha filled and must take none of alpha's static text out of them
deny out/none/html/beta.html `alpha shows` -- nor alpha's updater, which is the leak a shared per-window analysis would cause
deny out/none/html/beta.html `gamma body` -- gamma's text belongs to gamma's page
deny out/none/html/beta.html `gamma shows` -- and gamma's updater with it
deny out/none/html/gamma.html `alpha body` -- gamma reads caches alpha filled and takes none of alpha's static text
deny out/none/html/gamma.html `alpha shows` -- nor alpha's updater
deny out/none/html/gamma.html `beta body` -- beta's text belongs to beta's page
deny out/none/html/gamma.html `beta shows` -- and beta's updater with it
deny out/none/html/delta.html `alpha body` -- delta is generated last, after every cache is full, and still renders only its own tree
deny out/none/html/delta.html `beta body` -- same for beta's text
deny out/none/html/delta.html `gamma body` -- same for gamma's text
deny out/none/html/delta.html `function String` -- delta interpolates nothing, so it gets none of the script helpers the other three registered
deny out/none/html/delta.html `addEventListener` -- delta declares no handler, so any listener on this page would be another window's

-- site.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import nav "sngl:ui/nav"

output { none { html } }

var alphaCount = 0
var betaCount = 0
var gammaCount = 0

window(title=pages.current.title) {
    nav.stack #pages {
        nav.page #alpha(href="/", title="Alpha") {
            text(value="alpha body")
            button(text="press alpha", @click { alphaCount += 1 })
            text(value="alpha shows {alphaCount}")
        }
        nav.page #beta(href="/beta.html", title="Beta") {
            text(value="beta body")
            button(text="press beta", @click { betaCount += 1 })
            text(value="beta shows {betaCount}")
        }
        nav.page #gamma(href="/gamma.html", title="Gamma") {
            text(value="gamma body")
            button(text="press gamma", @click { gammaCount += 1 })
            text(value="gamma shows {gammaCount}")
        }
        nav.page #delta(href="/delta.html", title="Delta") {
            text(value="delta body")
        }
    }
}
